    "text": "<p>Two fair dice are thrown. The numbers on them are taken as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and a system of linear equations<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />is constructed. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is the probability that the system has a unique solution and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is the probability that the system has no solution, then:</p>"
